-- DAASI-3641 · PROD · RUN as plain steps, everything at once (Pete). The same change as DAASI_3641_PROD_2_RUN_STEPS.sql
-- without the canary: one run queues every broken BEM/WLM market trip (about 399,400) for the pipeline's own rebuild
-- and marks one rating on each matching property trip (about 923,500), and the next hourly run rebuilds them all.
-- Laid out like Marcin's April runbook: pause, back up, change, resume. Run one section at a time, in order; nothing to
-- edit. Start soon after the TIBCO tasks' 7:00 Pacific run: the hourly run after the change is the long one (hours),
-- the trip runs after it wait for it, and what reads the trip tables stays paused until it is done (step 11).
-- Chris's post-check, fix-up and undo work with it as with the RUN file (tag 'DAASI-3641 run 1 all', backups *_RUN1).


-- 1. Session
USE ROLE APP_SERVICE_PROD;                              -- owns the trip tasks, holds both writes
USE WAREHOUSE DAAS_PROD_ADHOC_BULK_LOAD_COMPUTE_XL;
USE SCHEMA DAAS_PROD.DAAS_BACKUP;                        -- where the temporary tables below go
ALTER SESSION SET TIMEZONE = 'America/Los_Angeles';    -- the trip tables' time zone

-- 2. Pause the trip chain and what reads it, as in April: the TIBCO tasks, then the dynamic tables, readers first.
--    Best a few minutes after an hourly run has finished (they end around :55 Pacific).
